  "status_text": "Use the whole drop budget of a circuit and the gates that flip bits give an exact countdown. Lean checked this for AND, OR and NOT gates that read at most two earlier wires, with two free constants. Read the b NOT outputs as a binary number, with the earliest gate as the most significant bit. The number never rises as input bits turn on and falls strictly when any wire turns off. If i successive drops can precede a selection and j can follow, the number is between j and 2^b-1-i. When i+j=2^b-1 it equals j (L-lib-1279).",
